        "original_id": "5b362386-e96d-56b4-9fc2-699076e84418",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stanley Elkin, Anne Lamott, Jack Shoemaker\n- Works: Mrs. Ted Bliss\n- Companies: Hyperion Books\n- Topics: American consumerism, popular culture, male-female relations\n\nFacts:\n- Stanley Elkin was born on May 11, 1930, and he was an American novelist, short story writer, and essayist.\n- Anne Lamott was born on April 10, 1954, and she is an American novelist and non-fiction writer.\n- Stanley Elkin's extravagant, satirical fiction revolves around American consumerism, popular culture, and male-female relations.\n- In 1995, Stanley Elkin died on May 31, and Hyperion Books published his novel Mrs. Ted Bliss.\n- Jack Shoemaker has published books by Anne Lamott and by writers including Guy Davenport, Romulus Linney, Gary Snyder, Wendell Berry, Evan S. Connell, MFK Fisher, James Salter, Gina Berriault, Reynolds Price, W.S. Merwin, Michael Palmer, Donald Hall, Kay Boyle, Gary Nabhan, Jane Vandenburgh, Carole Maso, and Robert Aitken.",
